    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0477" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/1195</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State
                            (White)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-15">October 15, 1931</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Guatemala, Dr. Recinos, and
                    the Minister of Honduras, Dr. Dávila,
                    called to exchange ratifications of the treaty and additional convention
                    regarding the arbitration of their boundary dispute. They exchanged the
                    ratifications and signed a protocol to this effect, copies of which they also
                    exchanged.</p>
                <p>They left with me a note to the Secretary of State enclosing copies of the Treaty
                    and Additional Act and asking that they be transmitted to the Chief Justice,
                    advising him of the exchange of ratifications and of his designation as
                    Presiding officer of the arbitral tribunal.</p>
                <p>Dr. Rowe was also present, as was Mr.
                        Sidney Smith.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rancis</hi>] W[<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">hite</hi>]
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
